as-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T16:24:42-07:00","id":1343882,"title":"","content":"What do spelling mistakes have to do with how long you've been thinking about something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T17:33:08-07:00","id":1343889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1343725#post1343725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm old enough to remember the Satanic scare in the 80s, and the argument some groups were making the argument that Dungeons &amp; Dragon's depictions of demons was endorsing satanism, and more than that, actually <i>encouraged</i> children to engage in satanic activities. So when somebody suggests that simple depiction = endorsement or encouragement, I just respond with a <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div> The thing to always remember when bringing up the Satanic panic is how that was a case of reactionaries thinking that a fictional depiction encouraged participation in a thing that <i>did not exist</i>. Fictional portrayal of things that categorically <i>do</i> exist needs to be treated with a bit more care.<br /> <br /> I feel as though any time somebody draws a comparison to the Satanic panic, they're implicitly cultivating a narrative of asserting that things such as misogyny, racism or {checks notes} support of torture are equally non-existent. If that's not a thing that they meant to do, that's just another example of the issues inherent to not fully considering what one says.<br /> <br /> Now, part of analysing Dresden Files is, well, misogyny there exists in more than just what Harry or any other character says or thinks. It ends up coming through in a lot of events and how women characters are framed or portrayed. If I gave Jim Butcher the benefit of the doubt, I'd say this is a case of unthinking repetition rather than reflecting an avidly held belief, but that still has issues that should be recognised. It does make it harder to buy misogynistic character statements as purely internal to the narrative, though.<br /> <br /> That's just a point I think hasn't been made yet, and others have already covered a lot of the intersection between depiction and endorsement.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","