 you found that one enlightening!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T10:41:22-07:00","id":1344985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement#post1343698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe that Depiction=Endorsement? And if you do,to what extent? Do you believe that every single creator approves of the actions of all of their characters? even the villains?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely not.<br /> <br /> And anybody who genuinely believes that needs to have a reality check. Stories need conflict, and that conflict can not exist unless you have both an antagonist and a protagonist to challenge each other.<br /> <br /> If you're going to accuse the writer of supporting the offensive content because they chose to add it to the story, then you would logically have to accuse the actors who agree to play the role of the villain of doing the same thing. After all, they agreed to play a misogynistic villain, so it's only logical that they must want to be a misogynistic villain, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:35:02-07:00","id":1345002,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://i.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/000/128/slowpoke.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T11:43:37-07:00","id":1345007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345002#post1345002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saying, he wasn't exactly able to post to this thread in the last few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:04:03-07:00","id":1345015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345007#post1345007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saying, he wasn't exactly able to post to this thread in the last few days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Yeah, good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:35:10-07:00","id":1345025,"title":"","content":"Joke's on you. I think Slowpoke is awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:29:36-07:00","id":1345042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345025#post1345025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joke's on you. I think Slowpoke is awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>I do too, I was just memeing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:04:49-07:00","id":1345092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1344985#post1344985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stories need conflict, and that conflict can not exist unless you have both an antagonist and a protagonist to challenge each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting a bit tangential... but no, dramatic conflict doesn't require conflict between a protagonist and an antagonist. Nor do the status of characters as protagonists/antagonists have anything to do with their moral character; simply that they're opposition and who the audience is following.<br /> <br /> To the first point, allow me to tell you the most famous flash fiction story in Western literature: &quot;For sale: baby shoes, never worn.&quot; Now, it does rely heavily on context to fill in some blanks, but the dramatic conflict is between aspirations/hopes/dreams/etc. vs. reality not going how you wanted it to go. The desire for a child is not the protagonist, nor is the mother, as they're never actually in the story, just inferred. The reality that the child wasn't born isn't an antagonist, and is also never actually directly in the text. However, the conflict between these two ideas is quite present, and quite dramatic.<br /> <br /> To the second point, in the opposite direction to an extremely long work in Western literature, we have the protagonist Jean Valjean vs. the antagonist Inspector Javert... but their conflict isn't actually the central conflict that makes the story pssible. While they do challenge each other, they serve more to challenge the audience directly with the, in D&amp;D terms, conflict between Lawful and Good; something neither of them actually resolves because it's a problem far beyond two men. The interweaving narratives of the rest of the characters is vital to making the story about more than two men at a philosophic impasse of what's a better way to act, but that society exists in a form where both men are wrong and right.<br /> <br /> Though both stories are still examples of depiction not being endorsements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:44:43-07:00","id":1345104,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Fair enough, but not everybody has the proper mindset to appreciate that kind of esoteric story telling. I can think of far, far, far, far more stories involving conflict between 2 or more sides, than I can about commenting on esoteric subjects like the inability to conceive healthy children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:51:12-07:00","id":1345106,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s not so \u201cesoteric\u201d to some of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:55:44-07:00","id":1345108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345106#post1345106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not so \u201cesoteric\u201d to some of us.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean in terms of thought provoking, or eliciting emotions.<br /> <br /> To me, it just makes me think <i>&quot;Oh, they couldn't have a kid. Okay, but I'm looking for a story with more action behind it.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:05:43-07:00","id":1345116,"title":"","content":"Not really sure where you're coming from regarding conflict.<br /> <br /> Not appreciating something doesn't mean the creator isn't endorsing it. Some people didn't catch on to Terry Goodkind's attempt to push Randian philosophy on anyone until his later books in the Sword of Truth series but it was still something he was trying to do, or when a tobacco industry (really, any industry) paid for product placement in movies or tv shows (and now, to celebrities) to promote their product as something cool people use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:35:03-07:00","id":1345122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345104#post1345104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, but not everybody has the proper mindset to appreciate that kind of esoteric story telling. I can think of far, far, far, far more stories involving conflict between 2 or more sides, than I can about commenting on esoteric subjects like the inability to conceive healthy children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, in many ways the protagonist vs. antagonist in direct conflict is the easier form of storytelling, and thus easier to come up with interesting forms of.<br /> <br /> But my point was that you're being prescriptive about what makes a story a story in a demonstrably wrong way. I felt it relevant to the topic because too many people think you &quot;need&quot; to include things, even though you actually don't, which is how people end up reaching for things like the Thermian Argument to justify inclusion in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:37:34-07:00","id":1345123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345108#post1345108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean in terms of thought provoking, or eliciting emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to some of us, there manages to be quite a bit of thought and emotions bundled up in those six words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345108#post1345108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, it just makes me think <i>&quot;Oh, they couldn't have a kid. Okay, but I'm looking for a story with more action behind it.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>In six words?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:49:19-07:00","id":1345125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345122#post1345122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But my point was that you're being prescriptive about what makes a story a story in a demonstrably wrong way. I felt it relevant to the topic because too many people think you &quot;need&quot; to include things, even though you actually don't, which is how people end up reaching for things like the Thermian Argument to justify inclusion in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, and there's plenty of art out there that would fall in line with such things. But I was more trying to point out the silliness of claiming that the presence of an antagonist advocates support of their ideals. As if the audience is forgetting that the story also features a protagonist who's ideological beliefs directly oppose those of the antagonist.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> Yes, such is often the case with patrons and students of the fine arts, who are able to recognize and interpret deeper meaning behind what they are being presented with. But then you have people who look at Picasso paintings and see nothing more than a chaotic, jumbled mess of shapes and colors.<br /> <br /> Art is subjective, and not everybody is capable of fully appreciating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T18:15:29-07:00","id":1345132,"title":"","content":"Sometimes protagonists and antagonists are <i>not</i> ideologically opposed, though; sometimes they\u2019d just rather have the MacGuffin more than the other guy, without giving a shit about what he believes in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-31-2019, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T18:47:49-07:00","id":1345141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345125#post1345125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true, and there's plenty of art out there that would fall in line with such things. But I was more trying to point out the silliness of claiming that the presence of an antagonist advocates support of their ideals. As if the audience is forgetting that the story also features a protagonist who's ideological beliefs directly oppose those of the antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>To sum up: You set up a strawman argument (i.e. \u201cthe presence of an antagonist advocates support of their ideals\u201d) and then your counter-argument to the strawperson was itself logically fallacious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-31-2019, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T19:46:46-07:00","id":1345145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345125#post1345125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I was more trying to point out the silliness of claiming that the presence of an antagonist advocates support of their ideals. As if the audience is forgetting that the story also features a protagonist who's ideological beliefs directly oppose those of the antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the story is advocating for the antagonist's ideals though. I brought up Javert because you are (and this is fairly explicit in the novel) supposed to agree with his ideals around the equal application of the law and how easily letting officers have too much power to interpret enforcement can undermine public trust in the law. Javert is an antagonist with ideals you're supposed to sympathize with and even agree with; even if not to the extent of agreeing with his methods.<br /> <br /> The Kingsman films both have villains that have laudable ideals (environmentalism, ending drug prohibition), but are evil because of their methods and savior complex egos.<br /> <br /> A lot of interesting antagonists are people you do agree with on some level, and that's on purpose.<br /> <br /> Or, simply put: authorial advocacy isn't linked to the character's narrative status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Art is subjective, and not everybody is capable of fully appreciating it. </div> </div> </div>Could you consider &quot;Art is subjective, and not everyone has the context to fully appreciate a given piece of art.&quot; as a different phrasing?<br /> <br /> While, yes, there's some people that literally aren't going to be capable of appreciating a given piece (such as a blind person and a painting), it shouldn't really be treated in this sort of elitist light that calling it a matter of capability makes it out to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:13:18-07:00","id":1345150,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Yes, that was the entire point I was trying to get at. If people are accusing the creator of supporting the material that they find offensive just because it was included, then how do they explain the creator also including content which is made to challenge, criticize and (in many cases) even defeat the offensive content?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> &quot;A lot of interesting antagonists are people you do agree with on some level, and that's on purpose.&quot; - Absolutely agree with this. In fact, I would say the best villains are the ones are the ones who you can find yourself agreeing with. They tend to stick with you long after they're gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you consider &quot;Art is subjective, and not everyone has the context to fully appreciate a given piece of art.&quot; as a different phrasing? </div> </div> </div>Not sure how this could be construed as elitism. There are simply forms of art that a lot of people either don't enjoy, or simply fail to grasp the meaning of.<br /> <br /> A lot of people think that Picasso is one of the greatest artists of all time, and pay lots of money to see exhibits of his paintings. But when I look at them, I just see a waste of good canvas. I don't understand what most of his work is supposed to be, and it fails to provoke any emotions from me besides confusion and apathy.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to music, I like rock, metal, and Celtic. But I am not a fan of rap, country, or anything that involves the vocalist screaming at the top of their lungs to the point where the words become unintelligible.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not saying people who enjoy the stuff I don't like should be ashamed of it, we simply have different tastes on the matter. My dad thinks Pink Floyd is one of the greatest bands of all time, but I personally find their music to be annoying to listen to. Their music was before my time, and whatever messages they sang about doesn't resonate with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2019, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:16:55-07:00","id":1345151,"title":"","content":"Small tangent, but I've long found it irritating that a piece of fiction - most often movies - will give the villain a chance to monologue about their ideology and reasons for doing evil, but the hero's only response is to punch them in the face. You so seldom get moments where the protagonist deconstructs the argument and refutes their point, like &quot;no, sir, you're wrong, and here's all the reasons why&quot;.<br /> <br /> Partly, this is a direct outgrowth of modern media's persistent pattern of Anti-Intellectualism. Wherein only bad guys &quot;overthink things&quot;, and it requires a no-nonsense person of action to &quot;cut through the bullshit&quot; and &quot;get things done&quot;. And where even non-villainous intellectuals are either reduced to ineffectual &quot;eggheads&quot;, are the supporting characters to protagonists-of-action, or are themselves so action-y that their intelligence is &quot;made up for&quot; by being so capable. (For more on this, see the <a href=\"https://youtu.be/RFBmM1HLooA\" target=\"_blank\">Renegade Cut episode on James Bond</a>.)<br /> <br /> However, the other reason I dislike this trend of setting up the villain's philosophy and then not deconstructing it is because it's too easy for an audience member who WANTS to agree with the villain (or who is merely receptive to the villain's ideas) to do so. Just look at how many people genuinely agreed with Thanos from Infinity War, about how overpopulation is a problem and that we need a purge. The Avengers et al., from what I understand from Endgame (I haven't watched it), don't ever really counter Thanos's ideas or point out the flaws. They just get a bunch of their people together and beat him up. Leaving the ideological question unanswered.<br /> <br /> (Of course, while Thanos's Neo-Malthusian ideas are wrong, what gets lost in the shuffle when it comes to discourse about the movie is that it was chosen, probably, out of a corporate desire to paint Environmentalism as villainous. A trend that we ALSO see in Hollywood. Just go back and consider how many villains in recent years were citing environmental concerns, or had an ecological bent to their ideology. This is not unintentional, I think. Big Business has a vested interest in demonizing opposition to Capitalist exploitation of the environment, even while at the same time corporations try to court ecologically-minded consumers with the <i>impression</i> of the companies also being ecologically-minded.)<br /> <br /> Returning to my point, it is very easy for a piece of media to convey or at least foster a message that has unfortunate consequences. An in-aptly told narrative or text can do so, even if the creators did not intend for it (let alone when they do). Which makes the trend of setting up a villain's philosophy and then not addressing it in the narrative - just assuming the audience can be properly horrified and not need correcting - quite problematic. Not necessarily because audiences are dumb (although the state of media and textual literacy is, itself, a problem), but rather because ideas can be latched onto quite easily with how influential media can be. The above-mentioned Infinity War has almost certainly created a whole new generation of Neo-Malthusians, for example, let alone what effects works like American History X have on the cultural landscape.<br /> <br /> To reiterate a detail that might get lost, <i>the author does not have to <b>intend</b> a reading for it to be accepted by some portion of the audience</i>. Milton certainly did not intend Lucifer to be seen in a positive light - being a good Christian writer - but that's a popular interpretation of Paradise Lost, much to Milton's chagrin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-31-2019, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:19:29-07:00","id":1345152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345150#post1345150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Yes, that was the entire point I was trying to get at. If people are accusing the creator of supporting the material that they find offensive just because it was included, then how do they explain the creator also including content which is made to challenge, criticize and (in many cases) even defeat the offensive content?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which might be a salient point if anyone in the history of media critique had ever made such an accusation. But not only is that not the case, but also your counter-argument to the imaginary accusation was factually wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-31-2019, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:26:11-07:00","id":1345153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345152#post1345152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which might be a salient point if anyone in the history of media critique had ever made such an accusation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought that's what the OP was asking about, and said they're seeing more of lately? Unless I misunderstood what they were asking about?<br /> <br /> In which case, I apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:54:08-07:00","id":1345158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345153#post1345153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought that's what the OP was asking about, and said they're seeing more of lately? Unless I misunderstood what they were asking about?<br /> <br /> In which case, I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is what they were asking about, yes. And the answer was a resounding \u201cyeah, nobody thinks that.\u201d Hence my slowpoke reaction image when you came in all \u201cAnyone who thinks that is wrong!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T21:18:23-07:00","id":1345162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345158#post1345158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is what they were asking about, yes. And the answer was a resounding \u201cyeah, nobody thinks that.\u201d Hence my slowpoke reaction image when you came in all \u201cAnyone who thinks that is wrong!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I understand now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T00:55:54-07:00","id":1345175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345150#post1345150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how this could be construed as elitism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of the word &quot;capable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Things like taste, preference, or whatever are not matters of capability. You might not like Picasso, but I believe that you could at least study his work well enough to understand why he's considered a master on an intellectual level even if such study doesn't lead to you liking his work. Saying you're incapable of understanding Picasso would be negative comment on your intellect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345151#post1345151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small tangent, but I've long found it irritating that a piece of fiction - most often movies - will give the villain a chance to monologue about their ideology and reasons for doing evil, but the hero's only response is to punch them in the face. You so seldom get moments where the protagonist deconstructs the argument and refutes their point, like &quot;no, sir, you're wrong, and here's all the reasons why&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with the main thrust of this, but I think there's some points unaddressed.<br /> <br /> First, there's a lot of movies that (at least attempt) to have the heroes show their response through their actions rather than through speech. The end of Captain America: the Winter Soldier doesn't have Natasha do a big speech to take deconstruct Pierce's arguments, but her actions to sacrifice SHIELD's secrets in order to expose Hydra, even to great personal expense, is a retort of it's own even if Pierce isn't around to hear it. Thor of all people is actually very prone to try to talk Loki into seeing reason rather than having to fight.<br /> <br /> Second there's also just a genre convention issue. Action movies don't leave a lot of narrative space for everyone to give big speeches. Unless there's purposeful deconstruction going on (Rorschach and Doctor Manhattan both get to say their piece in contrast to Ozymanius in Watchmen), you don't see it as much. It's fairly common in more traditional sci-fi (Star Trek does this enough TVTropes names it after Kirk, Star Wars does this a few times, the Atredies of Dune love doing this, and while I hate to give Card too much credit Ender certain gets one hell of a scene with this).<br /> <br /> Last, I think that some creators feel that the villain's speech is self-defeating enough that it doesn't need rebuttal. They don't need to have someone explain why Thanos's plan is nonsense because it's obviously nonsense... or at least it feels like the writers thought it would be. Going back a bit, you don't see people complaining that Loki's &quot;humans suck&quot; speech in Avengers didn't get more than pithy responses from an old guy and Cap, because it's clearly not a sound philosophy as performed. Going back to the original Kingman movie, there's a general sense that engaging with Valentine is kinda pointless on this level. He's right about climate change, but he's so far gone into the extremity of his solution, you're never going to talk him out of it. Having someone sit there an pick apart how wrong headed he is would feel redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T03:25:43-08:00","id":1345746,"title":"","content":"My two cents on the narrative of &quot;the Marvel movies don't do enough to refute Thanos' conclusions or motivations&quot;:<br /> <br /> One, they do more than nothing in having the charger of Gamorra, who probably had the deepest insight into his world view of anybody, when she calls it something insane and unfalsifiable. That scene also depicts the futility of doing so, as Thanos is impervious to such criticism with his certainty that he is not only in the right, but the only one capable of appreciating that and acting upon it. I will grant though that people aren't necessarily arguing that such a rebuttal would be for the benefit of him, rather than the audience.<br /> <br /> That leads to the second point of how the film didn't proactively affirm that his world view is correct. Maybe it being wrong is not in the text, but the subtext that the villain who is totally insistent that he's right and shrugs off any assertions that he isn't is not a credible advocate isn't exactly buried deep.<br /> <br /> Last is that Thanos isn't a political agitator, he's basically a terrorist. You don't really oppose people trying to implement their politics with violence by having a cordial debate with them, because it wouldn't accomplish anything anyway.<br /> <br /> I do get that the dramatic conventions of a movie, especially a comic book movie, can bend away from reality to have opposing characters express their viewpoints, but I think in a case like this it would still validate Thanos more than he deserves. Really, I think it says a lot more when heroic characters hear his motives and basically just roll their eyes at him.<br /> <br /> That said...<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345151#post1345151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small tangent, but I've long found it irritating that a piece of fiction - most often movies - will give the villain a chance to monologue about their ideology and reasons for doing evil, but the hero's only response is to punch them in the face. You so seldom get moments where the protagonist deconstructs the argument and refutes their point, like &quot;no, sir, you're wrong, and here's all the reasons why&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Depending on the genre of the movie, I think that in a lot of cases stopping to have an argument such as this would be kind of silly. But I see this as just a facet in the larger context of such films having a tendency to present the villain as the one with the proactive, transformative vision and the hero being somebody that is provoked to stop them and maintain the status quo. We don't really get much media that reflects the reality of villains as people who already sit in privilege at the top of unjust systems who act severely against folks who are proactively trying to change it for the better, and that probably is as a result of a motive to not alienate audiences (including those who might be on the side of the heroes but be frustrated at such narratives close to reality) as well as just general inertia in creative trends. I'd kind of blame the latter a bit more myself.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(Of course, while Thanos's Neo-Malthusian ideas are wrong, what gets lost in the shuffle when it comes to discourse about the movie is that it was chosen, probably, out of a corporate desire to paint Environmentalism as villainous. A trend that we ALSO see in Hollywood. Just go back and consider how many villains in recent years were citing environmental concerns, or had an ecological bent to their ideology. This is not unintentional, I think. Big Business has a vested interest in demonizing opposition to Capitalist exploitation of the environment, even while at the same time corporations try to court ecologically-minded consumers with the <i>impression</i> of the companies also being ecologically-minded.)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Eh, I think this is reaching a bit into the territory of conspiracy theory. These things don't need to be part of a secret plot to discredit a movement to show up in movies.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Buuuutttt\u2026</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Returning to my point, it is very easy for a piece of media to convey or at least foster a message that has unfortunate consequences.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This I agree with. Really, it's ultimately irrelevant whether or not a depiction connotes an endorsement, because our moral assessment of the creator is the least significant thing about it. There can still be depictions that are intended to read as bad but are still used irresponsibly.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T03:31:43-08:00","id":1345747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345175#post1345175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the original Kingman movie, there's a general sense that engaging with Valentine is kinda pointless on this level. He's right about climate change, but he's so far gone into the extremity of his solution, you're never going to talk him out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, it's kind of the neo-lib capitalist approach to climate change of a kind that one might almost expect to actually happen when the people responsible for it need to confront the reality to it. Don't agitate for regulations and renewable energy and material technologies and reducing the revenues of the oil industry; kill all the poor people.<br /> <br /> That would be a big part of why I wouldn't really buy the assertion that it's intended as a plot to demonise environmentalism, because... what, the audience is supposed to associate that movement with figures that, in real life, are often denying it? We're supposed to demonise and be afraid of the super billionaire? Yeah, no shit. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T03:37:34-08:00","id":1345748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345746#post1345746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last is that Thanos isn't a political agitator, he's basically a terrorist. You don't really oppose people trying to implement their politics with violence by having a cordial debate with them, because it wouldn't accomplish anything anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Looks at certain politicians)<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>You and I</i> don't, anyway...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T08:46:40-08:00","id":1345773,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> Kind of getting tired of people throwing the word &quot;terrorist&quot; around every time somebody does something remotely destructive.<br /> <br /> Thanos' absolute certainty that he is right in the MCU is demonstrably untrue. If his concern was that the universe didn't have enough resources, there are at least 3 stones on that gauntlet which could have resolved the problem without killing everyone.<br /> <br /> Time, Reality and Power!<br /> <br /> Time Stone - rewind the clock on all the harvested resources, so that they are back to full quantity. Don't tell me he can't do this, we saw Strange do it with an apple.<br /> <br /> Reality Stone - Make it so that the universes' resources are self replenishing, thereby giving people an infinite supply!<br /> <br /> Power - Solve the energy crisis in one fell swoop!<br /> <br /> This is why Thanos' reasons for wiping out half the universe was more believable in the comics. He wanted to impress Death, and believed destroying half the universe was the best way to do it.<br /> <br /> Changing him to some kind of environmental activist makes his whole plan look ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, did the MCU decide to can Adam Warlock? They teased him at the end of Guardians 2, and he was supposed to be the one who defeated Thanos in the comics. But he hasn't even gotten so much as a passing mention since they dropped his name at the post credits scene.<br /> <br /> Also, why didn't anybody use the time stone to save Tony? <i>&quot;Dormomu, I've come to bargain&quot;</i> ring any bells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:20:57-08:00","id":1345783,"title":"","content":"I think for the most part Marvel did a fine job of presenting Thanos\u2019 ideas as untenable. The one place they dropped the ball on it was having Gommorah\u2019s home planet become a paradise after Thanos killed half the people on it. Now, it\u2019s possible Thanos could have been lying about that, or talking out of his ass, but if so we should have been shown that it wasn\u2019t true. Otherwise the implication is that his idea would work, but shouldn\u2019t be enacted because it\u2019s immoral. And that\u2019s the wrong way to refute the idea, in my opinion. It would have been better to show, not just tell, that it wouldn\u2019t work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:40:28-08:00","id":1345788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345783#post1345783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for the most part Marvel did a fine job of presenting Thanos\u2019 ideas as untenable. The one place they dropped the ball on it was having Gommorah\u2019s home planet become a paradise after Thanos killed half the people on it. Now, it\u2019s possible Thanos could have been lying about that, or talking out of his ass, but if so we should have been shown that it wasn\u2019t true. Otherwise the implication is that his idea would work, but shouldn\u2019t be enacted because it\u2019s immoral. And that\u2019s the wrong way to refute the idea, in my opinion. It would have been better to show, not just tell, that it wouldn\u2019t work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another reason why it's untenable is that people have a tendency to BREED!<br /> <br /> Thanos didn't stop the depletion of the universe's resources, he only postponed it. And then destroyed the stones right afterward.<br /> <br /> What happens after a few hundred years or so, when the universe has had a chance to replenish its lost numbers? Is he going to wipe out half the universe again?<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, he can't...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T09:52:07-08:00","id":1345791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345788#post1345788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reason why it's untenable is that people have a tendency to BREED!<br /> <br /> Thanos didn't stop the depletion of the universe's resources, he only postponed it. And then destroyed the stones right afterward.<br /> <br /> What happens after a few hundred years or so, when the universe has had a chance to replenish its lost numbers? Is he going to wipe out half the universe again?<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, he can't...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you\u2019re going to try refuting his plan logically, it\u2019s far easier just to point out that smaller population size does not alleviate resource disparity. There are enough resources for everyone, they\u2019re just distributed poorly. Killing half the people wouldn\u2019t actually fix that problem. But again, logical refutation isn\u2019t really what was needed. The audience needed to be shown Thanos\u2019 plan not working. Film is a visual medium, if you want to convey a message through film you need to show it visually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T10:25:35-08:00","id":1345808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345791#post1345791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if you\u2019re going to try refuting his plan logically, it\u2019s far easier just to point out that smaller population size does not alleviate resource disparity. There are enough resources for everyone, they\u2019re just distributed poorly. Killing half the people wouldn\u2019t actually fix that problem. But again, logical refutation isn\u2019t really what was needed. The audience needed to be shown Thanos\u2019 plan not working. Film is a visual medium, if you want to convey a message through film you need to show it visually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Show, don't tell&quot;</i> as the rule goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:09:46-08:00","id":1345820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345773#post1345773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of getting tired of people throwing the word &quot;terrorist&quot; around every time somebody does something remotely destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of us are sick of people using this sort of language uncritically.<br /> <br /> MCU Thanos, by every reasonable definition of the word, was a terrorist. Using violence - esp. on civilian populations - to intimidate and coerce people into changing their existing government structures into the one desired by the violent actor? That's terrorism. That's what Thanos was doing until he focused on getting the stones: going to planets, using his overwhelming military power to crush their armies, and then brutally slaughter populations until they agreed to govern his way, before he'd move on. He was a terrorist. He just wasn't the current picture of a terrorist that's part of a small guerrilla paramilitary force.<br /> <br /> Even with the Snap, where he eschewed his normal hands on approach to reshape planetary civilizations, his goal was to violently induce change in how people operate (he wanted to terrorize the universe into avoiding overpopulation at all costs), and rejected other means of achieving his goals despite having nigh unlimited power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, did the MCU decide to can Adam Warlock? They teased him at the end of Guardians 2, and he was supposed to be the one who defeated Thanos in the comics. But he hasn't even gotten so much as a passing mention since they dropped his name at the post credits scene. </div> </div> </div>Can implies they got past the name drop stages at some point. Given the success of GotG and Ragnarok, it seems like they plan to do more of the galactic MCU in the future, and Adam is certainly a character to bring in if they do. But his &quot;default&quot; comics self is too tied to the Infinity Stones to bring him in as they were ending the Avengers movies. They need to figure out what to do with him (and Magus, his traditional nemesis rather than Thanos anyway) though, since there's major differences in the MCU from the comics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, why didn't anybody use the time stone to save Tony? <i>&quot;Dormomu, I've come to bargain&quot;</i> ring any bells? </div> </div> </div>Because someone still has to make Tony's Snap or it didn't happen in the main timeline, and you'd have two timelines one where his snap happens, and one where it doesn't... this is all fairly well explained in the movie.<br /> <br /> The climax of Dr. Strange worked because Strange put himself in a time-loop and the only way out was for Dormammu to bargain instead of trying to kill Strange again and reset the loop. Rewinding time just left the two of them on repeat, rather than changing the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T11:34:10-08:00","id":1345826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345783#post1345783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, it\u2019s possible Thanos could have been lying about that, or talking out of his ass, but if so we should have been shown that it wasn\u2019t true. </div> </div> </div> </div>I think we get more than enough characterisation for a person willing to give the material more than a surface level reading that Thanos is not really a credible witness to anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T12:59:38-08:00","id":1345856,"title":"","content":"RE: Terrorists<br /> <br /> I think it's a false objection to say that we shouldn't worry about villain logic going unchallenged because they're terrorists, and thus can be ignored. Different people consider the actions to be appropriate or inappropriate, depending on how correct they think the reasoning is or how &quot;necessary&quot; they think it is. One side's terrorists are another's freedom fighters, as the saying goes, and it can apply elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Thanos being a Neo-Malthusian terrorist doesn't really take the idea that much farther than Malthus himself did, as the latter openly advocated for purging the poor. Malthus wanted charity to be cut back and conditions in cities to be worsened, so that disease, civil violence, and hunger culled the ranks of the lower classes. THAT was his way of solving what he saw as a population crisis. Malthus was ALREADY an extremist. That extremism is <i>baked into</i> the philosophy.<br /> <br /> Which means when Infinity War/Endgame presents Thanos's Neo-Malthusian philosophy and doesn't address it, anyone who is receptive to the idea gets that idea either planted or reinforced in them. Far from being &quot;obviously and self-evidently wrong&quot;, a certain portion of the audience - as we've seen play out - will walk away from the theater believing this rhetoric. They've been given no reason to believe that Thanos's worldview is wrong, because the films don't present an alternative. This won't be true of every viewer, obviously, but enough people will believe it.<br /> <br /> Moreover, enough people will walk away believing that, while Thanos might have been wrong in execution, he might have had a point. These audience members won't walk away planning to commit terrorism, but they're still swayed to Malthusian ideology. An ideology that, as established previously, is both incorrect and dangerous.<br /> <br /> For another example, Eugenics. As explained in Spice 8 Rack's &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/U6LnVOV1SX8\" target=\"_blank\">Yawgmoth: The Scientific Priestcraft of Eugen!cs</a>&quot;, Eugenics did not die when the Nazis started a Holocaust in its name. The belief that certain people should not contribute to the genepool &quot;for the betterment of the human species&quot; (or that certain people should be favored for contributions because of &quot;good breeding&quot;) continued on for years and is still out there. Proponents simply rationalized that the Nazis &quot;took it too far&quot;, but still believe that Eugenics had merit. (For the record, it does not, and it's depressing we need to say that). Resulting in continued efforts throughout the 20th century, in otherwise &quot;polite&quot; societies, to restrict the rights of minorities in the context of reproduction, and passively by promoting ideas that certain people &quot;deserve&quot; to succeed and reproduce based on some inherent quality (an elitist belief that transcends normal Eugenics pseudoscience and into race, class, and culture).<br /> <br /> Just because terrorism is not advocated, does not mean spreading an idea cannot have malign effects. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345746#post1345746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think this is reaching a bit into the territory of conspiracy theory. These things don't need to be part of a secret plot to discredit a movement to show up in movies.<br /> <br /> Buuuutttt\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean to imply that there was a conspiracy behind making so many villains in media environmental extremists.<br /> <br /> It's just that, to quote Ross Scott (in his <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rxOKEsBx4NU?t=1713\" target=\"_blank\">review of Deux Ex</a>), &quot;ruthless, rich people tend to think alike&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heads of movie studios didn't all get together to ratify a compact, whereby they'll all endeavor to portray environmentalism in the worst light possible. It's just that the heads of major corporations tend to be highly personally invested in the status quo, and so are biased towards that status quo and against anyone or anything that &quot;rocks the boat&quot;. This manifests in the subtexts and messages that appear in the films they produce, which they tend to have final say over. In one case this involves making environmentalism look bad by having movie villains all be ecological terrorists. In another case, it's Disney repeatedly pushing a narrative that makes light criticism of Capitalism, while <a href=\"https://youtu.be/xU1ffHa47YY\" target=\"_blank\">laying the blame on individual people rather than systemic inequality</a>.<br /> <br /> (Although not coincidentally, both of those examples can be found in Disney in particular. So at least in this regard, the House of Mouse obviously has a self-serving agenda in all this).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:36:00-08:00","id":1345869,"title":"","content":"man,i'm trying really hard to believe Charlaquin and others are right. But by dear god,it's hard to deny that people indeed believe Depiction is Endorsement every time i take a cruise on the internet. <i>fuck me. </i>i've seen people calling whoever made Jurassic World a mysoginistic because there's a scene a woman is eaten by a dinosaur in that movie.<br /> guys... it's a monster movie! lots of people died,it's part of the story! it doesn't mean the guys believe that's right,they are just depiciting it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:40:37-08:00","id":1345870,"title":"","content":"hell,star wars is a hot button these days but i need to press it. People said rian johnson is racist because Finn shows up a littles less in the second movie than the second,and he has a funny scene at the beggining,let that sink in,<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:02:51-08:00","id":1345879,"title":"","content":"The misogyny (probably subconscious) isn\u2019t in that <i>a</i> female character was killed; it\u2019s in <i>how</i> female characters are presented in the film (though Zara\u2019s death scene isn\u2019t doing the movie any favors). <br /> <br /> Moreover, pointing out these problems is how we move past them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-04-2019, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:15:58-08:00","id":1345885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345869#post1345869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">man,i'm trying really hard to believe Charlaquin and others are right. But by dear god,it's hard to deny that people indeed believe Depiction is Endorsement every time i take a cruise on the internet. <i>fuck me. </i>i've seen people calling whoever made Jurassic World a mysoginistic because there's a scene a woman is eaten by a dinosaur in that movie.<br /> guys... it's a monster movie! lots of people died,it's part of the story! it doesn't mean the guys believe that's right,they are just depiciting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair though, the PA/babysitter death was kinda weirdly drawn out. More like the kind of thing that should have happened to D'Onofrio's character. I have never considered myself a feminist, but man, there was a weird motivation behind that death. Oh, and having BDH stay in high heels the whole time was odd too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:17:31-08:00","id":1345886,"title":"","content":"Your issue seems to be more listening to the opinion of everyone and attaching the opinion to multitudes of people. And specifically taking certain opinions (notably those that call someone out as being an 'ist' of some sort). There's almost 8 billion people in the world and most of them don't have an opinion on Star Wars or Jurassic World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:18:55-08:00","id":1345889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345879#post1345879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The misogyny (probably subconscious) isn\u2019t in that <i>a</i> female character was killed; it\u2019s in <i>how</i> female characters are presented in the film (though Zara\u2019s death scene isn\u2019t doing the movie any favors). <br /> <br /> Moreover, pointing out these problems is how we move past them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But don't you think the way all characters female or otherwise, are presented in any story are simply being part of the story being told,and not a showcase of the beliefs held by the story creators?<br /> I just dont think anyone can be a misogynist for simply making a movie,it takes more than that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:21:33-08:00","id":1345891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345886#post1345886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your issue seems to be more listening to the opinion of everyone and attaching the opinion to multitudes of people. And specifically taking certain opinions (notably those that call someone out as being an 'ist' of some sort). There's almost 8 billion people in the world and most of them don't have an opinion on Star Wars or Jurassic World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually,the posts I've seen have a lot of notes/likes/shares<br /> Somr number on the thousands","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:26:49-08:00","id":1345895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345891#post1345891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually,the posts I've seen have a lot of notes/likes/shares<br /> Somr number on the thousands</div> </div> </div> </div>They could have a million votes and it would still be less than .02 percent of people.<br /> <br /> You aren't obliged to agree with them. You aren't obliged to listen to them. You aren't forced to read anyone's blog entry or listen to anyone's video dissecting a movie. If you really have an issue with it, and you keep complaining about it, avoid it. But it wouldn't hurt to look into some criticism of literature and movies and be able to make informed decisions and analyses of things on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-04-2019, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:30:05-08:00","id":1345897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345820#post1345820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MCU Thanos, by every reasonable definition of the word, was a terrorist. Using violence - esp. on civilian populations - to intimidate and coerce people into changing their existing government structures into the one desired by the violent actor? That's terrorism. That's what Thanos was doing until he focused on getting the stones: going to planets, using his overwhelming military power to crush their armies, and then brutally slaughter populations until they agreed to govern his way, before he'd move on. He was a terrorist. He just wasn't the current picture of a terrorist that's part of a small guerrilla paramilitary force.<br /> <br /> Even with the Snap, where he eschewed his normal hands on approach to reshape planetary civilizations, his goal was to violently induce change in how people operate (he wanted to terrorize the universe into avoiding overpopulation at all costs), and rejected other means of achieving his goals despite having nigh unlimited power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to respectfully disagree there. Maybe it's because of the fact that, as Charlaquin pointed out, they did very little in the way of showing the results of Thanos' actions in detail. But it didn't seem like Thanos was using fear as a tool for controlling others. He did not tell people <i>&quot;do as I command, OR I'll destroy half your civilization.&quot;</i> he flat out explained himself as <i>&quot;I'm destroying half your civilization regardless, because that is the only rational course of action.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> There was no negotiation possible, no deal or payment his victims could offer that would stay his hand. And then, after wiping out half the universe, he almost immediately proceeds to destroy the stones and put his own life at risk doing so. Not even bothering to ensure that the rest of the universal governments lamented and agreed to follow his ideology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanos was an extremist, yes. Most certainly he was a zealot who deeply believed in his cause. But he was not a terrorist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-04-2019, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:35:46-08:00","id":1345899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345895#post1345895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They could have a million votes and it would still be less than .02 percent of people.<br /> <br /> You aren't obliged to agree with them. You aren't obliged to listen to them. You aren't forced to read anyone's blog entry or listen to anyone's video dissecting a movie. If you really have an issue with it, and you keep complaining about it, avoid it. But it wouldn't hurt to look into some criticism of literature and movies and be able to make informed decisions and analyses of things on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>it just that when someone attacks a creator especially a screenwriter ,it hits home. because i work hard every day at college to become a screenwriter,it's my life goal,to reach Hollywood and write the enxt big Script. To make a mark on human culture,it's my dream,the thing i want to do with my life.<br /> When someone attacks a screenwriter with a bad criticism,that ofte makes no sense and it boils down to mindless reasonless anger,it pisses me off. Because it feel slike they are attacking my dream","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:38:23-08:00","id":1345900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345889#post1345889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But don't you think the way all characters female or otherwise, are presented in any story are simply being part of the story being told,and not a showcase of the beliefs held by the story creators?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no fiction that exists <i>entirely</i> divorced from the beliefs held by the story creators. <br /> <br /> (I mean, shit, people keep making computer programs that end up having racial biases.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345889#post1345889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just dont think anyone can be a misogynist for simply making a movie,it takes more than that</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>did</i> more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:40:25-08:00","id":1345901,"title":"","content":"But it's even bigger than that. I found those criticisms of movie and creators,different than ones made 30 years ago. Honestly,and i admit this may be just being paranoid, it feels like every it passes,people become more extreme in their beliefs,crueler,more ruthless. At least,the people in the media. How many angry videos fill youtube? How many people who hate this or that are getting together to hate together?<br /> Hell,it feels like hate is the new drug of choice and it disturbs the hell outta me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:42:02-08:00","id":1345904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345889#post1345889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But don't you think the way all characters female or otherwise, are presented in any story are simply being part of the story being told,and not a showcase of the beliefs held by the story creators?</div> </div> </div> </div>A facet of a text does not need to be consciously crafted for it to exist in the text. Unconscious bias and preconceptions can inform decisions in the creative process. See also Coding.<br /> <br /> The exaggerated way in which a woman is killed in a film may arise from the filmmakers working on preexisting patterns. We see this more specifically in the frequency with which specifically Lesbians are targets of death in narratives. A pattern going back to earlier government mandated standards and practices within media, that compelled filmmakers to denounce and punish moral offenders within a narrative (and at the time (and still now, unfortunately) homosexuals were considered moral offenders that needed to be &quot;punished&quot; in stories). The standard was set, and then became inherited habit among filmmakers long after these restrictive standards and practices were removed, as a result of an industry that reinforces tropes and storytelling norms, regardless of utility.<br /> <br /> Creators continue to do these things - to women both generally and homosexual - out of unthinking adherence to existing ways of thinking. Of course it isn't conscious, because the filmmakers likely didn't even consider the issue to begin with when they made the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just dont think anyone can be a misogynist for simply making a movie,it takes more than that </div> </div> </div>On the subject of Misogyny and its pervasiveness, I point again at the Renegade Cut episode about James Bond (see the previous page for the link). He explains the nuances of Misogyny and how it can manifest in ways we don't normally think of when we think the word &quot;Misogyny&quot;. Suffice to say, Misogyny is more than merely hating women, and can manifest in subtle ways. Ways not even the creators themselves are aware of, because they have deep-rooted, unexamined biases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:44:25-08:00","id":1345905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345889#post1345889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But don't you think the way all characters female or otherwise, are presented in any story are simply being part of the story being told,and not a showcase of the beliefs held by the story creators?</div> </div> </div> </div>What beliefs the creators hold is irrelevant. What matters is the messages the stories send, intentionally or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345889#post1345889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just dont think anyone can be a misogynist for simply making a movie,it takes more than that</div> </div> </div> </div>Misogynist is an adjective, not a noun. While there are obviously some exceptions, most people don\u2019t actively hate women. However, we are all affected by the society we live in, which is systematically biased against women. We are therefore all liable to think and act in <br /> misogynistic ways from time to time, especially if we are uncritical of systemic misogyny within our culture. The same is true of any systemic prejudice. In general, intersectionalist critique of media is not made to call the creator \u201ca [whatever]ist.\u201d It\u2019s made to point out that certain aspects of the work, consciously or not, are [whatever]ist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:45:15-08:00","id":1345907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345899#post1345899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it just that when someone attacks a creator especially a screenwriter ,it hits home. because i work hard every day at college to become a screenwriter,it's my life goal,to reach Hollywood and write the enxt big Script. To make a mark on human culture,it's my dream,the thing i want to do with my life.<br /> When someone attacks a screenwriter with a bad criticism,that ofte makes no sense and it boils down to mindless reasonless anger,it pisses me off. Because it feel slike they are attacking my dream</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, then you should especially be learning about critical analysis. No movie is going to be above criticism but it would at least help you understand where some criticism is coming from.<br /> <br /> And yes, hate is popular, we have leaders gaining power because of it, and literal hate groups trying to hide their true stances because they know people will be more likely to reject their philosophies if they come out and be honest about it.<br /> <br /> As for differences between criticisms 30 years ago, you would still have people saying a movie is awful, they just wouldn't have a medium to get that across to people. Also worth noting, while the world population is almost 8 billion right now, it was just over 5 billion 30 years ago in 1989 (specifically the population was 5.198 billion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:46:10-08:00","id":1345909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345905#post1345905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What beliefs the creators hold is irrelevant. What matters is the messages the stories send, intentionally or otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Misogynist is an adjective, not a noun. While there are obviously some exceptions, most people don\u2019t actively hate women. However, we are all affected by the society we live in, which is systematically biased against women. We are therefore all liable to think and act in<br /> misogynistic ways from time to time, especially if we are uncritical of systemic misogyny within our culture. The same is true of any systemic prejudice. In general, intersectionalist critique of media is not made to call the creator \u201ca [whatever]ist.\u201d It\u2019s made to point out that certain aspects of the work, consciously or not, are [whatever]ist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. that i can get behind,it's just hard for me separatw legitimate people whose criticism are well meaning,and the hate mongers,and by god do i see a lot of hate mongers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 11-04-2019, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:50:57-08:00","id":1345911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345909#post1345909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. that i can get behind,it's just hard for me seprae legitimate people whose criticism are well meaning,and the hate mongers,and by god do i see a lot of hate mongers.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of that is just a result of access to global communication. There have always been and will always be people who hate any given piece of media, for any number of reasons, legitimate and not. It\u2019s just that the internet gives a platform to anyone and everyone who wants one. As a creator, it\u2019s important to be able to separate earnest criticism from mindless hate. Getting the two confused only leads to trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:57:10-08:00","id":1345914,"title":"","content":"all right.thanks for the answers so far guys.<br /> thank god my vacation is getting close,i'll have time to relax and think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:13:31-08:00","id":1345918,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <br /> <br /> While you shouldn't try to actively target people as grounds for prejudice, worrying about the subconscious biases is a tad ridiculous. Remember these ancient words of wisdom <i>&quot;you can't please everyone.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And besides, it's not as if cultural biases are objectively offensive. I'm pretty sure anybody who's ever listened to stand up comedy will attest to that. In the words of the late George Carlin <i>&quot;It all depends on how you construct the joke.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> When you create something based on the demands of a second or third party, we call that a commissioned piece. If your goal is to bring your own dream to life, then tell these hate mongers to either pay you for your time, or to fuck right off!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:57:26-08:00","id":1345931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345897#post1345897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to respectfully disagree there. Maybe it's because of the fact that, as Charlaquin pointed out, they did very little in the way of showing the results of Thanos' actions in detail. But it didn't seem like Thanos was using fear as a tool for controlling others. He did not tell people <i>&amp;quot;do as I command, OR I'll destroy half your civilization.&amp;quot;</i> he flat out explained himself as <i>&amp;quot;I'm destroying half your civilization regardless, because that is the only rational course of action.&amp;quot;</i><br /> <br /> There was no negotiation possible, no deal or payment his victims could offer that would stay his hand. And then, after wiping out half the universe, he almost immediately proceeds to destroy the stones and put his own life at risk doing so. Not even bothering to ensure that the rest of the universal governments lamented and agreed to follow his ideology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanos was an extremist, yes. Most certainly he was a zealot who deeply believed in his cause. But he was not a terrorist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very easy to find a common definition of the word &quot;terrorist&quot; denoting a person that employs unlawful violence, especially directed against civilians, in pursuit of a political aim.<br /> <br /> If a person shoots up or blows up a place of worship in a manner that was undeniably motivated by racial or religious bigotry (which is a political motive in and of itself), do we really need to debate whether their motive was to make other people of that demographic more scared or their motive was to make the ones right there dead before we call it an act of terrorism?<br /> <br /> Or, I mean, maybe you do, but most existing academics and authorities will find in principle that the &quot;make them dead&quot; motive constitutes terrorism. Especially if their political aim amounts to &quot;make the offending group not exist anymore&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T16:08:04-08:00","id":1345936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345931#post1345931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a person shoots up or blows up a place of worship in a manner that was undeniably motivated by racial or religious bigotry (which is a political motive in and of itself), do we really need to debate whether their motive was to make other people of that demographic more scared or their motive was to make the ones right there dead before we call it an act of terrorism?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Except once again, Thanos wasn't using fear as a tool for accomplishing his goals. The spreading of fear was purely coincidental with his actions. As I said, his first course of action after killing half the universe is to go back home, destroy the infinity stones, and settle down for the life of a simple farmer. He doesn't even try to double check his work and make sure everybody changed their behavior, he just has faith that everything will be better now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T16:41:38-08:00","id":1345947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345936#post1345936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except once again, Thanos wasn't using fear as a tool for accomplishing his goals. The spreading of fear was purely coincidental with his actions. As I said, his first course of action after killing half the universe is to go back home, destroy the infinity stones, and settle down for the life of a simple farmer. He doesn't even try to double check his work and make sure everybody changed their behavior, he just has faith that everything will be better now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you... believe that I'm in some way tricked by the fact that you've left out my first paragraph (&quot;violence against civilians in pursuit of a political goal&quot;) and my third one (&quot;academics and authorised regarding a politically motivated goal of making people dead as terrorism&quot;), which also put lines of the paragraph you've quoted into the proper context?<br /> <br /> Because you've certainly not addressed those points. You're just repeating the same assumption that something is only ever terrorism if it is intended to promote fear.<br /> <br /> The point of what I'm saying about the unfortunately not hypothetical shootings of mosques and synagogues and blowing up of African American churches is that the distinction between &quot;make the survivors scared&quot; and &quot;make the dead a thing&quot; need not be sussed out, because it is irrelevant. It's terrorism either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:03:14-08:00","id":1345951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345918#post1345918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> <br /> <br /> While you shouldn't try to actively target people as grounds for prejudice, worrying about the subconscious biases is a tad ridiculous. Remember these ancient words of wisdom <i>&quot;you can't please everyone.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And besides, it's not as if cultural biases are objectively offensive. I'm pretty sure anybody who's ever listened to stand up comedy will attest to that. In the words of the late George Carlin <i>&quot;It all depends on how you construct the joke.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Let me reiterate, I do not care what the creator thinks. Whether they are consciously biased, subconsciously biased, or anything else, I don\u2019t give one wet fart what the creator thinks. The creator\u2019s thoughts and opinions do not matter. The messages their works send matter. Similarly, I don\u2019t care about offense. People may be offended or not offended by just about anything, it\u2019s a terrible basis on which to critique creative works, especially because often times you need to offend certain people to send a strong message. What I care about is the tangible effects of a work. The messages it sends, the harm or the good that it does. Please, please, try to understand, individuals\u2019 thoughts and opinions have next to no bearing on my critical analysis of creative works. I know it can be hard to shift one\u2019s way of thinking from an individualistic basis to a systemic basis, but please believe me when I tell you, individual perspectives are just not a factor in my critical analysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345918#post1345918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When you create something based on the demands of a second or third party, we call that a commissioned piece. If your goal is to bring your own dream to life, then tell these hate mongers to either pay you for your time, or to fuck right off!</div> </div> </div> </div>...What the heck are you going on about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-04-2019, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:08:25-08:00","id":1345952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345947#post1345947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you... believe that I'm in some way tricked by the fact that you've left out my first paragraph (&quot;violence against civilians in pursuit of a political goal&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I simply clipped the part I felt like addressing, because it seemed to be the most relevant to the point I was trying to make. But even then, my point stands. He wasn't driven by politics, or anything of the sort. He was driven by concern for the environment, which stemmed from first hand experience of what happens when the people failed to heed his warnings. Terrorists make demands, they threaten, they coerce, they use intimidation to force people into compliance.<br /> <br /> Thanos didn't do that, killing half the universe was neither a bargaining chip, nor was it a means to an end. <b>It was the end itself,</b> and he was going to do so regardless if people agreed to change their ways. And immediately after he succeeded in doing so, he hung up his hat and quietly retired. At that point, he had no ship, he had no army, and he had no stones. If the universe wanted to keep going about things the way they had been doing, there wasn't a lot he could do to stop them.<br /> <br /> And if convincing people to change their ways was his main goal, then all he needed to accomplish that was the Mind Stone, since it contains the power of every conscious life form in the universe. He could have just used it to force people into compliance via mind control.<br /> <br /> Thanos didn't care about getting people to change their ways, he cared about the threat of overpopulation making society unsustainable. So he set out to destroy half the universe's population in an effort to save people from a self inflicted apocalypse. An apocalypse which had already befallen his own people, after they failed to heed his warnings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:20:13-08:00","id":1345957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345951#post1345951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...What the heck are you going on about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Merely trying to say that they should focus on creating art that they can feel proud of, and not allow the outrage from others to hinder their creative process. Unless they're offering to hire you for a story that they want to read, fuck 'em.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, this is probably why some actors and writers like to follow people around and study their behavior, in order to get things as accurate as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:54:49-08:00","id":1345967,"title":"","content":"Minecraft is not a game about colonialism.<br /> <br /> And yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/d6i5Ylu0mgM\" data-code=\"d6i5Ylu0mgM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/d6i5Ylu0mgM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I agree with Dan(on the whole, but I'm gonna dig into the particular of it happening)-no one intended for that narrative to emerge-but it happens.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, Minecraft's accidental colonialist message is not a deal breaker or major message, and there are a lot of media pieces that have similar problems that are also not going to direly affect the way people think about the world-but a lot of other unintended messages are harmfully propagated wide and far before someone takes catches it as well.<br /> <br /> The accidental nature of that messaging, in either case, is more problematic than a deliberate implementation of it. A deliberate implementation happens either because a) a person who deliberately puts forward a problematic concept in media/um often does so because their point is to highlight it and comment on it, and ultimately use the media/um as a way to ultimately demonstrate the problems of that concept, or b) legitimately believes in it's implementation, and has it's sincerity show up on it's sleeves in it's own way in such a way that blood and bone will clearly find their own.<br /> <br /> Accidentally messaged things, by contrast, is hard to deal with because it's harder for creators or readers to admit to and own because the other points come across more strongly, and the ignorance of basically everyone makes it harder to admit that a problematic narrative emerged out of something else. It is not as apparent even when it happens. So people can walk away with a reinforcement of any number of values, many of which can be toxic or otherwise negative, without ever confronting it, and when confronted with it have an easy time just dismissing it, or even getting critically defensive of it.<br /> <br /> Now once that's done, okay, it happens, people make mistakes, things slip through the cracks. It's <i>bad</i>, but in an ideal situation, the creators will own the problem and course correct in some way going forward, or at least, you know, apologize for it. The end goal is to get participants in (a) media/um, both creators and consumers, to examine their biases that they might not otherwise have credited affecting their work or reading, and at least decide for themselves how they let the reading go from there.<br /> <br /> The problem, then, is when creators don't do any of that, and when the fans of a property go long and far in defying the acknowledgment of any such flaws in media. When given the chance to take their passive participation in the creative and consumptive process, they instead lash out and allow what is basically a societal poison or disease to spread because the alternative is somehow uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> As a more at-home example, I love the fuck out of Beast, and I always have-but it started off with some really bad messaging that was not intended, and part of what it is now is because Beast still has some uncomfortable ideas at play in it's narrative. The primary difference is that Beast has owned a lot of the really bad unintended-but-emergent narrative that presented, worked hard to erase the most unneccesary elements of it, and has refined the rest of it into part of it's point as playing a villain for fun and psychologically healthy reason while still keeping the meta-narrative clear that it's current problems are to be seen as problems and not, you know, something to praise and defend.<br /> <br /> If Beast had continued onward with it's original draft and just dug in deep to that, I couldn't defend it now that I'm aware of what the hell I was missing in that first draft, and probably wouldn't touch it. But I stepped back, learned from those who had gripes with it, and saw a better Beast than the one I originally read. So far, Beast since has been working towards that, and heaven knows I'm gonna keep it up where I'm involved.<br /> <br /> But anyways, yeah, people absolutely write messages they didn't intend, and we as the audience absolutely ingest it as well.<br /> <br /> The average person eats 8 spiders while they sleep. Passive media creation and consumption is much the same thing-taking in something you might not want to while you just sleep-watch a show. With responsible media creation and consumption, you want people to at least have the option of knowing what they're eating (and possibly telling other people to eat) as much as possible, at the least.*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345951#post1345951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...What the heck are you going on about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have questions about this question and I feel they can be inferred from me mentioning that I have them.<br /> <br /> *Also, Hey Lie vs Awakening from Mage: the Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:52:14-08:00","id":1345994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345952#post1345952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He wasn't driven by politics, or anything of the sort. He was driven by concern for the environment</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanos didn't do that, killing half the universe was neither a bargaining chip, nor was it a means to an end. <b>It was the end itself,</b> [...] Thanos didn't care about getting people to change their ways, he cared about the threat of overpopulation making society unsustainable. So he set out to destroy half the universe's population in an effort to save people from a self inflicted apocalypse. </div> </div> </div> </div>You've just contradicted yourself twice.<br /> <br /> Environmentalism is a political goal. Like, basically everything that a person wants that pertains to how people act and society is structured is political, but if it needs to be something that carries the trappings of politicians then there are still things like Green Parties and then manner in which its a major focus on both sides of the American political aisle.<br /> <br /> You say that killing half the universe was not a means to an end, and then describe the end it was a means to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrorists make demands, they threaten, they coerce, they use intimidation to force people into compliance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they just kill the people they view their politics as incompatible with.<br /> <br /> You &quot;clipped the past of my post relevant to the point you're trying to make&quot;? Person, the point you're trying to make is not correct. The parts of these last two posts you keep evading are describing that fact, and here you are again insisting on a definition of terrorism that is wrong.<br /> <br /> At least have the fortitude to say that you don't think the events I referred to of the politically motivated murder of people in places of worship qualify as acts of terrorism.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hey, does everybody remember how Guardians of the Galaxy used the actual word terrorist to describe Ronan the Accuser, a man whose motive through the entire film is to write out the population of a whole planet in fulfillment of a cultural imperative (i.e. for politics)? I guess they must have deleted the scene where he &quot;um, actually&quot;'d the Nova Force with the fact that he wasn't trying to demand, threaten, coerce or intimidate the people of Xandar into complying with his political goal of them all not living anymore, he just went after them with a super-nuke to do it himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-04-2019, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:00:35-08:00","id":1345995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345994#post1345994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At least have the fortitude to say that you don't think the events I referred to of the politically motivated murder of people in places of worship qualify as acts of terrorism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I do that? It absolutely is terrorism. &quot;convert or die, heathen.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's completely different from <i>&quot;there are too many people. I'm going to kill half of you.&quot;</i> And then afterward deciding <i>&quot;There, I killed half the universe. Now I can dismantle my WMD's and settle down to grow my own garden. No need to bother with setting up a new infrastructure to make sure I don't have to do this again.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:26:03-08:00","id":1346001,"title":"","content":"So, uh, this episode of Renegade Cut just dropped: &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/X-8ICfWsUVw\" target=\"_blank\">The Problem with Rick and Morty</a>&quot;.<br /> <br /> I thought it was pertinent to the discussion, RE: the difference between a creator's intended meaning and the work's <i>textual</i> meaning. And how that can teach dangerous lessons, when there is a segment of the audience receptive to the lesson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-04-2019, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:28:19-08:00","id":1346002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1345995#post1345995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would I do that? It absolutely is terrorism. &quot;convert or die, heathen.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so despite your protests to the contrary, you actually are in a space of &quot;we have to speculate on whether or not the motives were about scaring the living rather than creating the dead in order to call it terrorism&quot;.<br /> <br /> That and the apalling naivete of thinking that a person who shoots up a mosque or synagogue would provide the option of conversion, or care much if somebody did.<br /> <br /> Also that one thing, kind of small so easy enough to miss, just a trifle really along the lines of <b><i>YOU CAN'T CONVERT OUT OF BEING BLACK!!!</i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-04-2019, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:28:48-08:00","id":1346003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346001#post1346001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh, this episode of Renegade Cut just dropped: &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/X-8ICfWsUVw\" target=\"_blank\">The Problem with Rick and Morty</a>&quot;.<br /> <br /> I thought it was pertinent to the discussion, RE: the difference between a creator's intended meaning and its textual meaning. And how that can teach dangerous lessons, when there is a segment of the audience receptive to the lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now I've got something to watch after my game upkeep. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:30:47-08:00","id":1346004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346003#post1346003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now I've got something to watch after my game upkeep. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. It was honestly quite fortuitous, that the video got released at this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:53:50-08:00","id":1346012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346002#post1346002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, so despite your protests to the contrary, you actually are in a space of &quot;we have to speculate on whether or not the motives were about scarring the living rather than creating the dead in order to call it terrorism&quot;.<br /> <br /> That and the spelling naivete of thinking that a person who shoots up a mosque or synagogue would provide the option of conversion, or care much if somebody did.<br /> <br /> Also that one thing, kind of small so easy enough to miss, just a trifle really along the lines of <b><i>YOU CAN'T CONVERT OUT OF BEING BLACK!!!</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>I never</b> protested to the contrary... It seems you are missing my point entirely. The people killing churches due to religious motivations are terrorists, because they are using the threat of violence to forcefully convert people to their own way of thinking. And sure, they probably don't offer the victims the chance to convert. But that's not necessarily their goal. Getting the survivors to convert is what they're probably going for. <i>&quot;Abandon your false gods, or this will happen to you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Thanos is not a terrorist, because he doesn't care if you agree with his way of thinking. He's going to kill half the universe indescriminatly, regardless if anybody thinks he had the right idea or not. There is no negotiation to be had, no payment to be offered. Just a man on a mission, who's already made up his mind. Are people afraid of him? Yes, duh! Who the hell wouldn't be?<br /> <br /> But is their fear something that he aspires to capitalize on? No, it is simply a side effect of him doing what he feels is necessary to save the rest of the universe. And once he has successfully done so, he steps away and lets people continue to go about their lives as normal.<br /> <br /> By your argument, we could say that Galactus is a terrorist, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-04-2019, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T21:33:56-08:00","id":1346041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346004#post1346004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem. It was honestly quite fortuitous, that the video got released at this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just watched it.<br /> <br /> Yeeeeaaaaaah count me as one of those people who got caught up in the idea about Rick being unhappy as part of the point. To me (prior getting a lot of this pointed out), it wasn't so much that Rick was right or cool or intelligent or often the winner-it's that none of that made him happy. I think there is a decent subtext to everything to reinforce that, and a really interesting series of analytics for it...<br /> <br /> ....buuuuuuut Yeah, I'm pretty sure the Pickle Rick By T-Shirt Guy at McDonald's didn't get that read, and honestly a lot of the assholes who like Pickle Rick have decent reason not to read it that way. It's not a major read of the story in comparison to everything else. And really, the rabbit hole of my own read goes down to unhappiness as an inevitable end of confronting reality while still supporting the authenticity argument for experience, so basically it's just a story about how we're fucked.<br /> <br /> I'ma still watch Rick And Morty, because it's funny and I can't escape my own read on it and find it helpful for prioritization-and also because it's great cathartic transgression-but I'm gonna keep this in mind as I do so.<br /> <br /> Also I need to get around to watching Always Sunny and Bojack Horseman. and Steven Universe, for some reason that came to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T21:50:57-08:00","id":1346045,"title":"","content":"I'll definitely agree that you need to watch Steven Universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:09:08-08:00","id":1346053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346045#post1346045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll definitely agree that you need to watch Steven Universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> EDIT: Nevermind, took ArcaneArts off my ignore list, so I could read their comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-05-2019, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:20:09-08:00","id":1346056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346041#post1346041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I need to get around to watching Always Sunny and Bojack Horseman. and Steven Universe, for some reason that came to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always Sunny does some things very well, but I couldn\u2019t get past the transphobia. It was only a couple of episodes, but the completely ruined the show for me. I haven\u2019t watched BoJack either, but I hear good things. Watch Steven Universe. It is so, so good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T03:58:14-08:00","id":1346117,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346045#post1346045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll definitely agree that you need to watch Steven Universe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346056#post1346056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always Sunny does some things very well, but I couldn\u2019t get past the transphobia. It was only a couple of episodes, but the completely ruined the show for me. I haven\u2019t watched BoJack either, but I hear good things. Watch Steven Universe. It is so, so good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I've heard that Bojack seems to have been canceled? Not sure if they managed to salvage its contract, or not?<br /> <br /> I enjoy Steven Universe as well. The series has a slow burn, and gradually goes from a monster of the week adventure, to something with a more overarching plot. Most of the characters are likable... except for the Diamonds... Pink Diamond especially...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-05-2019, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T04:19:27-08:00","id":1346122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346012#post1346012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>I never</b> protested to the contrary... It seems you are missing my point entirely. The people killing churches due to religious motivations are terrorists, because they are using the threat of violence to forcefully convert people to their own way of thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a remarkable talent for simply ignoring large sections of my posts as to not engage with points that I'm making. I put the reference back to the matter of an African American church being bombed and how your thesis of &quot;this stuff is terrorism when the motive is to compel conversion&quot; (which is still wrong) does not intersect with it at all, and it's just invisible to you.<br /> <br /> So let's set aside the violence directed towards Jewish and Muslim people (and the fact that those identities run deeper than one's specific religious practices, especially to the bigots that target them with harassment and violence) and focus specifically on white supremacists who target African American people with murderous violence.<br /> <br /> It is a fact that these people are motivated by the non-existence of black people, as can be seen not only in the fact that they keep trying to murder them, but their own rhetoric that casts the matter as a struggle for survival that only one can come out of. When a person commits murder, particularly mass murder, of African American people motivated by nothing more than their deaths, that is terrorism.<br /> <br /> Can you respond to that point at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting the survivors to convert is what they're probably going for. <i>&amp;quot;Abandon your false gods, or this will happen to you.&amp;quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, do you not know the first thing about Nazis? Do you honestly think that the anti-Semitism of them or anybody else is motivated by religion? When they're going on about goddamn racial purity and international finance and great replacement conspiracy theories? You think if George Soros converted to Christianity, everybody who makes a big song and dance out of loathing him and scapegoating him would just stop?<br /> <br /> <br /> But is their fear something that he aspires to capitalize on? No, it is simply a side effect of him doing what he feels is necessary to save the rest of the universe. And once he has successfully done so, he steps away and lets people continue to go about their lives as normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By your argument, we could say that Galactus is a terrorist, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Galactus is motivated by his need to eat to survive.<br /> <br /> I notice that you're also completely evading my description of you as having made several contradictory points earlier. Your whole &quot;he's not political, he's just an environmentalist&quot; thing. Nothing to say about that?<br /> <br /> You know, I find that there's a deeper point that I've been overlooking. Sure, the desire to murder people indiscriminately as an expression of a political motive is terrorism, but this whole argument started because you said you were sick of people calling things terrorism that you thought were not.<br /> <br /> What were you actually thinking of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:30:48-08:00","id":1346134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346122#post1346122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have a remarkable talent for simply ignoring large sections of my posts as to not engage with points that I'm making.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where as you seem to have a remarkable talent for using mental gymnastics to try and twist my argument to suit your own narrative. I was originally going to write a whole rebuttal to this comment. But by the time I got to the end, I realized it was veering things waaaaay of track from the original purpose of this thread. <br /> <br /> Find somebody else to be your sound board, I'm not engaging in this argument any further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:38:55-08:00","id":1346168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346117#post1346117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I've heard that Bojack seems to have been canceled? Not sure if they managed to salvage its contract, or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, last I heard is that the 6th season will be the last.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1346117#post1346117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I enjoy Steven Universe as well. The series has a slow burn, and gradually goes from a monster of the week adventure, to something with a more overarching plot. Most of the characters are likable... except for the Diamonds... Pink Diamond especially...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, chalk that up to the production drama. The show was conceived as a serial, but networks generally prefer series marketed towards children to be episodic. So, the first season was almost completely episodic, with only the barest hints of an overarching plot. Then they got renewed for a second and third season, which later got divided into two smaller seasons each, and expecting this to be all they were going to get, they made a plan to do as much of their planned story as they could in the time they had, though they still had to fight to get the network to let them serialize it, which is part of why even the later, more plot-heavy parts of the show are laden with filler episodes. Sadly, the diamonds\u2019 character arcs had to be rushed to fit them in with all the constraints they were working under. Except Pink\u2019s, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T23:23:49-08:00","id":1428058,"title":"","content":"i just saw someone talking about joss whedon on another thread and i felt the need to bring this thread back,as fair i know there's no rules against that.<br /> <br /> The three main criticism of the first two avengers movies all hit on the Depiction is not Endorsement button.<br /> There's criticism of Loki calling Black Widow a archaic word for bitch. people forget the fact Loki is a villain ,an power hungry jealous conqueror with very little morality. of course he'd have no calms on using misogynitisc terms<br /> Tony Stark makes a rape joke on Age of Ultron,it's the same principle, the whole point of MCU Tony is that he is a very toxic guy,due to being raised by distant parents,losing said parents at a young age and having more money than what he knows what to do with. he's trying to unlearn this behaviour,but he's still a deeply flawed human being,it makes sense he'd make a cruel joke<br /> And of course,there's Black Widow being said about being infertile,people have said Whedon was calling infertile woman monsters. Again,blackw idow has been indocritnated by a very terriblegovernment,brutalized and experimented on,it makes sense she'd have self loathing views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T03:17:02-08:00","id":1428071,"title":"","content":"Characters are not always mouthpieces for an author or director. Just because a character says something in a book or a movie or a video game doesn't necessarily mean that the creator agrees with the views of that character. Sometimes maybe they do! For example J.K. Rowling (rightly!) got slammed pretty hard because her own views on transgender individuals, and then you can see the way transgender individuals in her books are treated and talked about and it becomes clear that the writing there is intended to be a mirror into Rowling's own personal feelings.<br /> <br /> What's important is if you can find a pattern in the way certain characters are treated in an author's work, or if you can find the author making their own personal opinions. But if it's just a one-off or even two-off scene where a character (especially a villain or character of dubious morality) does or says something problematic, then it's a bit dangerous to immediately jump to thinking that that character is a mouth-piece for the author.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't know much about the Joss Whedon thing. I've seen a few of his movies and TV shows. But I have heard that his ex-wife came out and said that he has said some fairly misogynistic views about women though Whedon said that there were lots of inaccuracies in her statements and that she was mad over his infidelity. In such a situation it's fairly easy for people to believe whatever they prefer to believe, that Whedon's wife is wrong and Whedon isn't a misogynist, or that his ex-wife is right and he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T04:05:40-08:00","id":1428076,"title":"","content":"The accusations about how Joss behaves outside of the public eye are significantly older than the Avengers. The majority of it is also focused on off-camera issues (which as I noted in the other thread, is part of the problem, how he treats women off-screen is at direct odds with the values he says he wants to guide his depictions of them on-screen).<br /> <br /> Charisma Carpenter, who worked on Buffy for four years,and then Angel for four more, had to finish her run on the show coma acting for most of her last season before getting written out of the show... because Joss was unhappy with Charisma getting pregnant. While Joss did deny that was the reason, almost no fans bought his statement; esp. since movies and TVs have been hiding pregnancies from audiences for decades through costuming, props, and angles, her character's departure was a (almost literal) deus ex machina, and left multiple plots unresolved despite Joss saying that her character's arcs were all sufficiently explored.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding his divorce, one of the biggest pieces of evidence of him being misogynistic was that he publicly touted the success of their marriage as being due to his feminist values teaching him how to properly respect his spouse, while he was cheating on her (and he has admitted that he cheated on her repeatedly). Even if that doesn't cross into full misogyny for anyone's reading of events, he's still an open liar and hypocrite specifically regarding his treatment of women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T08:45:20-08:00","id":1428096,"title":"","content":"i feel like this threa,and my feelings about whedon are starting to be part of bigger problem. i'm 24 and yet i feel much,much older. the stereotype of an oler person who saw the word pass by and doesn't understand anything anymore. i remember being a teenager and opening up social media and understanding things,things made sense. now everything seems so skewed,sometimes even morally skewed. i suppose it's possible i'm giving him one too many chance,but it's hard to see such an immense amount of hatred and think it's justified. people have said some truly cruel stuff and about this particular dude and it's hard not feel sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T10:23:55-08:00","id":1428106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1428058#post1428058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's criticism of Loki calling Black Widow a archaic word for bitch. people forget the fact Loki is a villain ,an power hungry jealous conqueror with very little morality. of course he'd have no calms on using misogynitisc terms<br /> Tony Stark makes a rape joke on Age of Ultron,it's the same principle, the whole point of MCU Tony is that he is a very toxic guy,due to being raised by distant parents,losing said parents at a young age and having more money than what he knows what to do with. he's trying to unlearn this behaviour,but he's still a deeply flawed human being,it makes sense he'd make a cruel joke<br /> And of course,there's Black Widow being said about being infertile,people have said Whedon was calling infertile woman monsters. Again,blackw idow has been indocritnated by a very terriblegovernment,brutalized and experimented on,it makes sense she'd have self loathing views.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I do think there's a place for fiction in which characters that are supposed to be terrible are depicted without a filter so it can go into the weeds of them doing or saying really reprehensible things in a context where there's a catharsis or the audience being expected to properly engage with how much the people on display are real bastards (although even then some things need to be handled responsibly).<br /> <br /> I don't think mass market comic book movies are quite the place to do that. Things that are being put out to enormous audiences of families, of kids. From reasons ranging from having a certain tonal dissonance to maybe casting a wide net that can catch people off guard with things that are unnecessarily uncomfortable or harmful to associating things with characters that impressionable sections of the audience might engage with in fairly straightforward ways.<br /> <br /> There are alternative ways for characters to be cruel or traumatised than having them display direct misogyny, and Tony Stark is a well-liked character several steps above him being a problematic person for reasons including his snark or edgy jokes and it's maybe a good idea to exercise some responsibility in how you compose the things about him that kids might think of as cool and want to emulate.<br /> <br /> I can't recall if I've already said it in this thread, but part of the problem with its premise is that depiction and endorsement are kind of a false dichotomy. It's possible to depict a thing with the specific purpose of condemning it even, and do a bad job of that in a manner that makes it a kind of tacit endorsement even when not intended, as well as the degree to which a poorly framed condemnation can hurt people who'll have traumatic experience with it.<br /> <br /> These are all points that can be made without having anything to do with Joss Whedon's inner heart or personal worldview (although there's a matter in which greater insight into these things might raise a question of how accidental any of this might be, or inversely one could notice underlying misogynistic elements in his general writing or showrunning that lends credence to the idea that his feminism is quite flawed at best).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T10:49:47-08:00","id":1428109,"title":"","content":"I mean, you seem to appreciate him as a film creator, and you said yourself you wanted to get into film. No one is saying 'Buffy is retroactively bad now' but it does seem like you're sort of conflating the guy with his creations just like you complain about others doing the same. Most of the complaints we've noted here have been aspects of his personal and professional life, not his creations. They are not about Buffy the tv show, or the Avengers movies as they came out in theaters. If you can believe that &quot;He made this happen in the movie, but he does not really believe it&quot; you should be able to appreciate that &quot;In order to make something like his work, you don't have to be like him personally.&quot; Because if he's not bringing his personal views, then you can toss those aside and just appreciate his work for what it is.<br /> <br /> It's great that you can be so optimistic about the creators you like. Joss Whedon's not the only or first, you've also mentioned JK Rowling and started this thread talking about rpg industry folk. But it might be easier for you if you appreciated more that a creator is not their work, and so an aspersion against a Creator is not an aspersion against Media You Like. And just like it's okay for you or me to still enjoy Buffy, it should be understandable if someone else doesn't want to watch it or has lost interest in it, because people are going to care about things differently.<br /> <br /> All that said, studies have shown social media leads to a wide range of mental health issues, from depression and anxiety to loneliness and lower self esteem and worse. You do often come here complaining about seeing negative stuff 'all over' and things like 'immense hate' while I hope you're exaggerating (Joss Whedon hasn't been in the news or trending for months now), pairing that with missing the more topical criticisms it does seem like you might be seeing this stuff because of who and where you're getting your information. There are a lot of groups out there that try to shut down and mislead about any criticism for their own agendas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2020, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T18:20:53-08:00","id":1428141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1343698-do-you-believe-that-depiction-equals-endorsement?p=1428109#post1428109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is saying 'Buffy is retroactively bad now' but it does seem like you're sort of conflating the guy with his creations just like you complain about others doing the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't quite phrase it like that, but I actually was in a camp of &quot;let's critically revaluate the quality of Buffy's feminism and other general features&quot; even before there became more widespread word on what he might be like as a person and a figure on-set and in production.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it might be easier for you if you appreciated more that a creator is not their work, and so an aspersion against a Creator is not an aspersion against Media You Like.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could go even further and say that critical analysis, even of a kind that judges a work to have flaws, is not the same as casting aspersions.<br /> <br /> But critical analysis also tends to at least consider the traits of the creator that might inform the text or lend it context. Creative works still emerge from the world view and decision making of the creator, those things are interlinked.<br /> <br /> Death of the author is useful as a tool for saying that the creator is not the sole or ultimate authority on how their work is to be interpreted, for reasons including that it can have significance in a context they did not mean, it includes perspectives and biases unconscious to the creator, or that the major point of interpretation is how it makes the audience feel rather than what was meant by the creator. It's not really functional as a premise for one justifying to themselves not wanting to engage with the possibility that problem creators lead to problem art.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that people should be forced to make such evaluations if they just do not have the energy for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}